  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_048: multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → acc 0.520), the largest remaining uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion actually adds value over a strong unimodal baseline. Config_022 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer) is a clean ablation: it keeps the same image encoder and aggregation strategy as config_048, removing only the RNA modality and fusion step. If image-only performs comparably (~0.52), the RNA contribution is marginal and I should redirect remaining budget toward unimodal optimization or simpler multimodal variants. If image-only is substantially worse, it confirms that multimodal fusion is worth pursuing and justifies investing the remaining 7 experiments in refining the multimodal configuration (encoder choices, aggregation, fusion). This single experiment resolves the highest-impact design question before committing further budget."
}

